    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "settings": {
        "caption": "Common questions",
        "heading": "Before you order",
        "heading_size": "h1",
        "heading_alignment": "center",
        "layout": "section",
        "container_color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "open_first_collapsible_row": true,
        "image_ratio": "adapt",
        "desktop_layout": "image_second",
        "padding_top": 52,
        "padding_bottom": 52
      },
      "blocks": {
        "faq-sizing": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which size should I order?",
            "icon": "ruler",
            "row_content": "<p>Order the size that matches your usual shoe size. If you are between sizes, or you wear a wide fit, size up. The size range for each item is listed on its product page. Still unsure? Email us your shoe size and we'll tell you which to pick.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-shipping": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does shipping take?",
            "icon": "truck",
            "row_content": "<p>Delivery times vary by item, so we don't quote a single window. You'll get a tracking link by email as soon as your order ships, and you can follow it the whole way. Shipping is free on US orders over $50.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-pre-order": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Not sure which one to order?",
            "icon": "chat_bubble",
            "row_content": "<p>Email us before you order. Tell us your shoe size or what you're looking for and we'll tell you which option fits — it's much easier than guessing and sending something back.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-materials": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are they made of?",
            "icon": "leaf",
            "row_content": "<p>It varies by range. Compression socks and sleeves are a bamboo or nylon blend knitted with spandex. Toe spacers and separators are soft silicone. Braces and splints use a stretch fabric with hook-and-loop straps and a moulded support panel. Insoles use an EVA foam base with a breathable fabric cover. The exact materials for each item are listed on its product page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-shoes": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which items can I wear inside shoes?",
            "icon": "shoe",
            "row_content": "<p>Insoles, socks, foot sleeves and toe spacers are made to be worn inside everyday sneakers, work boots and most closed shoes. Insoles are trim-to-fit along the printed guide lines, and are a tight fit in dress shoes and flats with a shallow footbed. Night splints, knee and ankle braces, stretching straps and massagers are used out of shoes — each product page says which applies.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq-sizing",
        "faq-shipping",
        "faq-pre-order",
        "faq-materials",
        "faq-shoes"
      ]
